    {
      "id": "claim_aedd14b9db374e368121eca2d6766e5c",
      "statement": "tabId flows through three layers: the tool layer normalizes input and rejects non-string/empty tabId with invalid_tool_input; page-actions.ts resolves tabId ?? config.defaultTabId into the WebSocket request options; and websocket-client.ts targetEnvelope only adds a target object to the envelope when browserInstanceId or tabId is present. On the extension side, BrijioBackgroundController.handleSocketMessage calls extractTabId(message) which reads message.target.tabId (string) and parses it to a number for browser APIs, returning undefined when absent.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/shared/src/background-controller.ts#L564-L644",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:478c4973c56b92ec3f9f569a3178e62ff687d528093704620f4bb9bd5111fada:"
