        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_3cea2ec2b25945b892596a5e3b7583e4",
      "statement": "The open_tab tool does NOT accept a tabId parameter because it creates a new tab rather than targeting an existing one. It validates the URL scheme (parseUrl rejects non-HTTP/HTTPS with unsupported_scheme) and returns { tabId, url, title } where title may be empty until the page loads. The returned tabId must be passed to subsequent reads/actions because the new tab may not be the active foreground tab. close_tab and ownership tracking are deferred to P2.5.",
      "evidence": [
