    {
      "id": "claim_132931d82db54732a0207d8dc8b20633",
      "statement": "On success capture_screenshot returns MCP content with an image block ({type:'image', data:<base64>, mimeType:'image/jpeg'}) and a text block with JSON metadata (width, height, tabId, capturedAt). The extension strips the data:image/jpeg;base64, prefix. Chrome and Safari return width:0/height:0 in the current implementation. When the extension lacks a PageScreenshotAdapter the controller responds with capability_not_supported; runtime permission errors map to capability_not_supported, other failures to capture_failed.",
      "evidence": [
